d a plan  to create an alternative option for  families desperate to avoid sending  their kids to Camden's traditional  public schools  I signed though five hundred parents  through an idea she got deeply involved  in building political support for the  state's first charter school  authorization bill when things got  difficult what I called the parents here  I come for the legislature every time  the devel came up in committee there I  was with buses of parents in 1996 the  Charter School bill passed and leap  became one of the first to open in New  Jersey located in trailers on a vacant  lot on the Camden waterfront it was  about bringing leadership leadership to  have the guts to say what matters here  is the children and we're going to  create a school system that is gonna  work  and we're gonna hold teachers  accountable when they tell the union's  hell no you're not gonna run our schools  today leap occupies five modern  buildings in downtown Camden offering  its 1,500 students a cradle till college  education to to the third and then not  only did every kid get into college last  year some are attending the top schools  I get only 70% of the per pupil cost I  can then guess well I get 15,000 per  child Condon gets twenty eight well with  that money I get to pay mortgages I get  to pay books I get to pick teachers  wonderful salaries these are the seconds  squared  it's not just about having things but  also about feeling things feeling  important they mean that you could work  to get all these things everybody else  has all these people want to solve  poverty before you solve schooling  schools or institutions we control and  that's what I feel like we need to be  doubling down I'm there every day every  day  don't let anybody ever tell you what  your life is supposed to be like not a  teacher not your friends not your family  members there's so many things that are  blocking you from getting to where you  want to be but hard work and education  will break through any wall it'll bust  through any glass ceiling there's  absolutely nothing that can stop you if  you invest in yourself that's my song a  lot of children has been killed and I  look at their pain and the hurt on their  faces and I don't want that I don't want  my son to get caught up in the wrong  anything
 

